  "headline": "On 10,483 US high school students in 2025, a model trained on 2023 students using only digital-life answers (social media use, sleep and online bullying) sorted who had felt sad or hopeless with an AUC of 0.65 (0.64 to 0.67). Sex and grade alone scored 0.62. Sleep showed the clearest steps: 54% of students sleeping 4 hours or less felt sad or hopeless, against 24% at 8 hours. 40% of those on social media more than once an hour did, against 23% of non-users and 25% to 32% in between. In NHANES adults aged 18 to 24 (the public file has no PHQ-9 answers under 18), a PHQ-2 of 3 or more caught 59% (51% to 68%) of those with a PHQ-9 of 10 or more.",
